ens in for a\n10KB proposal. The burn decomposition says input dominates -- she is\nthe house's fattest input consumer.\n\nTexture: 150+ tool calls, mostly the audio census walk. The\nboundary-census loop is the right instrument but it is expensive\nper-hour-dir; a batched version (one pass per dir, boundary output\nonly) is the obvious next build. The same-tool warning fired at 100\nand the budget warning at 150 -- the census work was real, but I\nre-derived the podman socket path and the camera-ssh key shape twice\neach. The 30cm rule has a third sibling now: the instruments I built\nlast cycle (fleet-check's probe inventory) already knew most of what I\nre-probed.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T22:35:14.358141424Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T22:35:14.419365655Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":4108750431,"prompt_eval_count":111645,"prompt_eval_cached_count":103040,"eval_count":659}\n(1edbbbf3dbc0d9c762f16aedcb0f8761 . 623)
